          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grand Performance: Cegorach's Jest" hidden="false" id="7981-22a5-7b15-0205" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Grand Performance: Cegorach's Jest" id="92e6-0844-4038-82e9" hidden="false">
                  <description>*Voidweavers and Skyweavers burst toward their prize, evoking Cegorach's attempt to steal an antler of Kurnous.* Pivotal Roles: 1 Troupe Master, 1 Skyweaver Jetbikes, 1 Voidweaver. Additional Players: +3 Harlequin Troupes, +1 Death Jester, +1 Shadowseer, +2 Skyweaver Jetbikes, +2 Voidweavers. The Last Laugh: At the end of the game, the Controlling Player gains +D3 Victory Points if they have three or more units of Starweavers, Voidweavers, or Skyweaver Jetbikes (in any combination) in the opposing player's Deployment Zone. Amateur Performance: If, at the end of the game, there are no Starweaver, Voidweaver, or Skyweaver Jetbike units in the opposing player's Deployment Zone, the opposing player gains +D3 Victory Points.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grand Performance: Cegorach's Lament" hidden="false" id="3371-c0cd-10ff-e37b" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Grand Performance: Cegorach's Lament" id="d465-21c2-212a-ecc7" hidden="false">
                  <description>*The Harlequins embodied the tragedy of the Fall through lightning-fast, bloody revenge on She Who Thirsts.* Cannot be selected in the same army as a Detachment with the Traitor Allegiance. Pivotal Roles: 1 Troupe Master, 1 Harlequin Troupe, 1 Arebennian. Additional Players: +2 Harlequin Troupes, +2 Death Jesters, +1 Shadowseer, +1 Skyweaver Jetbikes, +2 Voidweavers. The Curtain Falls: At the end of the game, if Rillietann-only units have destroyed three or more units with the Daemon or Daemon Primarch Unit Type or the Corrupted Sub-type, the Controlling Player gains +D3+1 Victory Points. If the Arebennian slays the enemy Warlord during the game, the Controlling Player gains +2 Victory Points. If the enemy Warlord is removed by any other means, no extra Victory Points are gained, but the Amateur Performance penalty does not apply. Amateur Performance: If, at the end of the game, no Victory Points were scored from The Curtain Falls, the opposing player gains +D3 Victory Points.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grand Performance: Faolchu's Blade" hidden="false" id="e9d1-2dc0-1ac0-9cc6" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Grand Performance: Faolchu's Blade" id="7310-5435-ae7c-171e" hidden="false">
                  <description>*Starweavers and Voidweavers descended relentlessly, embodying the Great Hawk's consort bearing Anaris to Eldanesh.* Pivotal Roles: 1 Troupe Master, 1 Harlequin Troupe, 1 Skyweaver Jetbikes. Additional Players: +2 Harlequin Troupes, +2 Shadowseers, +2 Skyweaver Jetbikes, +2 Voidweavers. The Falcon's Wing: All Infantry models with this rule must begin the game embarked on a Transport. Before the game, count the units with Independent Character in the Controlling Player's Primary Detachment. At the end of the game, if at least half of them (rounding up) are still in play, and at least one friendly unit with The Falcon's Wing is still in play, the Controlling Player gains +D3+1 Victory Points. Amateur Performance: If, at the end of the game, no Victory Points were scored from The Falcon's Wing, the opposing player gains +D3 Victory Points.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grand Performance: The Heroes Path" hidden="false" id="0603-1004-0a85-bef9" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Grand Performance: The Heroes Path" id="2d33-9890-3979-a8c9" hidden="false">
                  <description>*Warriors embodying Ulthanash and Eldanesh burst from the shadows, though terrible pride gnawed at the hearts of the daring.* Pivotal Roles: 2 Troupe Masters, 2 Harlequin Troupes, 1 Shadowseer. Additional Players: +2 Harlequin Troupes, +1 Death Jester, +1 Shadowseer. The Sin of Pride: All Character models with this rule must issue or accept any Challenge whenever possible. At the end of the game, if these models have destroyed three or more models in Challenges, the Controlling Player gains +D3 Victory Points. Amateur Performance: If, at the end of the game, no models have been destroyed in Challenges by Character models with The Sin of Pride, the opposing player gains +D3 Victory Points.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grand Performance: The Trials of Khaine" hidden="false" id="7066-31b7-e635-f10b" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Grand Performance: The Trials of Khaine" id="d9b8-a704-9a35-6842" hidden="false">
                  <description>*Embodying the war god's ordeals against the Yngir, the Harlequins became death and slaughter given form.* Pivotal Roles: 1 Troupe Master, 2 Harlequin Troupes. Additional Players: +2 Harlequin Troupes, +1 Death Jester, +1 Shadowseer, +1 Skyweaver Jetbikes, +1 Voidweaver. The Bloodied Blade: At the end of the game, if Rillietann-only units have destroyed three or more units in the Assault phase, the Controlling Player gains +D3 Victory Points. Amateur Performance: If, at the end of the game, no units have been destroyed in the Assault phase by Rillietann-only units, the opposing player gains +D3 Victory Points.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
      </selectionEntryGroups>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
