  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Aeldari (X)" id="53d5-0ff0-0729-ab6c" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>The civilization keywords represent the major surviving branches of the Aeldari species. Every Aeldari unit has at least one Civilization keyword, shown as X, which determines which armies, detachments and force organizations may include that unit. These keywords work like Legion, Klan or Household affiliations in other factions. Aeldari units may only be selected in armies whose Civilization keyword matches at least one of the unit's listed Civilization keywords unless specifically stated otherwise. Units with several Civilization keywords may be selected in any army matching one or more of them: a Corsair Voidreaver unit with the keywords Anhrathe and Asuryani may be selected in either an Anhrathe army or an Asuryani army; a Harlequin Shadowseer with the Rillietann keyword may be included only in armies permitted to include Rillietann units; an Incubi unit with only the Drukhari keyword may only be selected in a Drukhari army. Unless specifically stated otherwise, Asuryani and Drukhari units may not be selected within the same Primary Detachment; Rillietann units may be included as Allied or Auxiliary units in any Aeldari army; and Anhrathe units may be selected as Primary, Allied or Auxiliary forces alongside either Asuryani or Drukhari armies.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rillietann" id="a1fb-e585-7858-f5e5" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>- Has the Fear (1), Furious Charge (1), Hit &amp; Run, and Move Through Cover Special Rules. - May only be taken in a Saedathii Detachment. - A Rillietann model with Independent Character may only join units that also have the Rillietann Sub-type.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Agent of Pandemonium" id="abea-9928-da39-be13" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>The model gains the Phantasmancy Psychic Discipline, plus the Thaumaturgy and Telepathy disciplines from the Core Rulebook (page 322).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bio-Explosive" id="984c-01d4-eaee-1efa" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>If a model is slain by a weapon with this rule, centre a Small Blast (3") marker over it. All models under the marker suffer an automatic hit at Strength 5, AP 4, with Ignores Cover. Models slain this way do not generate further Bio-Explosive markers.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dimensional Edge (X)" id="94b5-123e-7ada-142c" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>A weapon with this rule only ever wounds on the value X. No Saves or Damage Mitigation rolls of any kind may be taken against its Wounds.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Embrace of Death (X)" id="4474-fd98-1741-111e" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>A model attacking with a weapon with this rule makes X attacks with it at Initiative step 10, regardless of its Attacks and any bonuses (including Charging). The weapon may only be used in the first round of a combat, and may be used even after a Disordered Charge.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ghostlight" id="ce12-efa1-32aa-1eb1" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>When a unit with more than one model armed with Ghostlight weapons shoots, it may combine its fire. Select one model; no other model in the unit may fire a Ghostlight weapon that phase. The selected model shoots with its Ghostlight weapon (if it has several Ghostlight profiles, choose one; if only one profile has Ghostlight, use that one). For every two additional models in the unit with a Ghostlight weapon that can see the selected model, apply one of the following bonuses (the same bonus may be chosen more than once): - +6" Range. - +1 Strength (to a maximum of 10). - –1 AP (to a minimum of 1). - +1 shot.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Harrow-Lord" id="7e68-431d-89c2-6f52" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>Any unit that loses a model as a casualty in the Shooting phase to an attack from a model with this rule must take a Morale check as if it had suffered 25% casualties.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Monofilament" id="0f99-0b63-d7df-512d" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>When rolling To Wound normally against a non-Vehicle model, use the target's Initiative instead of its Toughness; Toughness still decides Instant Death. Any unit hit by one or more Monofilament attacks takes an Initiative test once the attack is resolved. If failed, it reduces its Initiative and Movement by 2 until the end of its Controlling Player's next turn. These penalties are cumulative and apply to later Initiative tests, but models with a starting Wounds of 6 or more cannot have their Characteristics reduced this way.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Open-Topped (X)" id="e049-003c-17ef-9739" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>Up to X models Embarked on a Transport with this rule may shoot in the Controlling Player's Shooting phase, measuring from the hull. They count as having moved, which may stop some weapon types firing. Abilities that replace a Shooting Attack (such as Psychic Powers or Cybertheurgic Rites) may not be used. These shots may target a different unit from the Transport's, but Reactions to them target the Transport. Rules that let a unit count as Stationary (such as Relentless) do not apply while embarked. Rolls on the Vehicle Damage table against this model add +1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ponderous Aim" id="c1ef-e23a-a5eb-123b" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>A weapon with this rule cannot be fired as part of a Reaction or used to Snap Shoot.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Skilled Rider" id="45f6-e922-2622-e9e2" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>The model may Run in the Movement phase and still fire a single ranged weapon in the Shooting phase, at BS 2. These To Hit rolls cannot be improved by any source. A unit that uses this rule may not use Firing Protocols (X) in the same Game Turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Soul Forfeit" id="edc1-998a-31b3-888d" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>The model never awards Victory Points when slain, and does not count towards units slain at the end of the battle. It does not count as a Scoring or Denial unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Transport Skiff" id="ea7c-8af2-2663-4f04" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>The model gains Infantry Transport and Assault Vehicle, and counts as a Vehicle for those rules and the Transport Sub-type. When it loses its last Wound, all models embarked suffer a S6, AP – hit, allocated by the Controlling Player. Survivors are placed where the model was (or as close as possible) in coherency and at least 1" from enemies; any that cannot be placed are removed. The unit then takes a Pinning test.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Vortex" id="c76f-9574-1148-443e" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>Once an attack with this special rule has been fully resolved, any Blast markers placed as part of that attack are not removed from play and instead are left in place for the remainder of the battle. Such a Blast marker is then referred to as the Vortex marker. The area under a Vortex marker is treated as Area Terrain for the remainder of the battle, and applies the following effects to all models that enter its boundaries: No line of sight may be drawn through, into, or out of the area covered by the Vortex marker (as such, models within such an area of terrain cannot draw line of sight to any other model, nor can other models draw a line of sight to them). Any models that enter the boundary of this area of terrain, or begin the Movement phase of the model's Controlling Player within its boundaries, immediately suffer one Str 10, AP 1 Hit and the Instant Death and Armourbane (Melee) special rules. If the model has the Vehicle Unit Type and suffers a Penetrating Hit due to this effect then it adds a modifier of +3 to that roll on the Vehicle Damage table. This area of terrain does not confer a Cover Save and no model within its boundary may use a Cover Save granted by any other rule or effect.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="c6b6-7283-ea8c-50d8" hidden="false" publicationId="307a-4562-12d7-0868">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
